        using ADDHLD = Field<_BTR4, 4, 4>; // Address-hold phase duration These bits are written by software to define the duration of the address hold phase (refer to Figure81 to Figure93), used in mode D or multiplexed accesses: For each access mode address-hold phase duration, please refer to the respective figure (Figure81 to Figure93). Note: In synchronous accesses, this value is not used, the address hold phase is always 1 memory clock period duration.
