        using BKP = Field<_RTC_BKP20R, 0, 32>; // The application can write or read data to and from these registers. They are powered-on by VBAT when VDD is switched off, so that they are not reset by System reset, and their contents remain valid when the device operates in low-power mode. This register is reset on a tamper detection event, as long as TAMPxF=1. or when the Flash readout protection is disabled.
